  "methodology": {
    "erasure_handling": "Missing/unreadable bits are marked as None (erasure). BER is computed over non-erased bits only. Erasure rate is reported separately.",
    "frame_check": "Bio.Align.PairwiseAligner (global NW, match=1, mismatch=-1, gap_open=-2, gap_extend=-0.5). Checks whether every codon-start in the original maps to a codon-aligned position in the noisy sequence. CONSERVATIVE GATE: if any codon-start is displaced, all n_bits positions are marked as erasures. The aligner maps positions; it does not restore deleted bases or perform error correction.",
    "indel_limitation": "At 0.5% per-base indel rate, the probability that at least one codon-start is displaced in a 600+ nt gene is high. Most trials fail the frame gate \u2192 100% erasure. This correctly reflects physical reality. ECC and synchronisation recovery (Person 2's backend) are required to improve indel robustness. RS ECC alone does not solve frame realignment.",
    "aggregation": "macro-average across all test genes (each gene contributes equally regardless of length)",
    "ecc_applied": false,
    "ecc_note": "Reed-Solomon ECC is in Person 2's backend. These results are raw extraction. RS ECC alone does not solve frame realignment \u2014 the backend must also implement synchronisation recovery and a codon-position to RS-symbol mapping."
  },
